# Creating illustrations

Follow these steps to go from a message to a finished illustration. Each step links to the page with the detail.

## 1. Decide the message

Write the task the illustration explains in one sentence, such as “Put the hall sensor away from the radiator.” If the main point is a number or a trend, use a [chart](brand-data.html) instead.

## 2. Gather reference

Look at photos of the real room and device. Note what is in front, what is behind and how big the key object is. Ignore the styling: you only need the structure.

## 3. Sketch the scene

Block in the large shapes first. Find the main action and make it the focal point. Check that the sketch reads at a glance.

A scene can be one object, such as a smart plug, or a whole room. Choose with the questions in [Choose an approach](illustration-principles.html#choose-an-approach).

## 4. Simplify the shapes

Reduce each object to its simplest shapes, in flat colour and a flat view. [Illustration principles](illustration-principles.html) sets the style, and [Objects and props](illustration-objects.html) shows how to simplify a device.

## 5. Build the composition

Decide what to keep, what to simplify and what to remove. Show depth with simple layers, not a 3D view. [Layout of a scene](illustration-layout.html) explains overlap, space and framing.

## 6. Add people

If the scene needs people, follow [Characters](illustration-characters.html) and [Hands and gestures](illustration-hands.html).

## 7. Set the hierarchy and colour

Make the key object the largest or the strongest shape. Use plain space to separate it from the background. Take colours from [Illustration colours](colour-illustrations.html), which sets the base colour and how many colours to use.

## 8. Review the illustration

Check that the illustration:

- reads at small and large sizes
- uses the same shapes and colours as other civica illustrations
- has no detail that does not explain the action
- avoids every [incorrect approach](illustration-incorrect.html)

Then export it and run the checks in [File formats and exporting](illustration-formats.html#check-the-file).
